usb: add RTL8188EU USB Wi-Fi device model (usb-rtl8188eu) with a virtual station bridged to a netdev

--- /dev/null	2026-09-17 07:51:14.703064162 +0200
+++ b/hw/usb/dev-rtl8188eu.c	2026-09-17 07:51:20.193062032 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,1861 @@
+/*
+ * Realtek RTL8188EU USB 802.11n adapter -- device model with a built-in
+ * "virtual station" that associates to the software AP run by the guest
+ * driver (rtl8188eu v5.x, e.g. hcRTOS/hccast) and bridges its data traffic
+ * to a QEMU netdev.
+ *
+ * What is modelled:
+ *  - USB 2.0 device: vendor control requests 0x05 (register read/write and
+ *    8051 firmware download), bulk OUT (TX descriptors + 802.11 frames),
+ *    bulk IN (RX descriptors + 802.11 frames, TX reports), interrupt IN.
+ *  - The MAC register file (64 KiB, byte granular) with the behaviour the
+ *    driver polls for: power-on state machine, EFUSE reads, firmware download
+ *    handshake, LLT init, H2C mailboxes, CAM polling, RF serial interface.
+ *  - A single associated station: open-system auth, association, WPA2-PSK
+ *    4-way handshake (CCMP), MAC-NAT bridging to the netdev peer.
+ *
+ * Not modelled: real crypto on the data path (the driver uses hardware
+ * encryption, so frames pass the USB boundary in the clear anyway),
+ * rate control, power save, 11n aggregation.
+ *
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 Edis Kazaz
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+
